        "thesis pp115-116,124 Figure 4.4",
        "thesis physical p240 / C13 Table C2"
      ],
      "finding": "Article methods: 2.0 g, 250 mL 0.5 M H2SO4, 3 h. Article Figure 4b: 2.0 g, 250 mL 1 M acid. SI Table S2: 0.5 M and treatment token 3 (x 2)) + 2. Thesis methods: 5.0 g, 250 mL 0.5 M, 3 h; thesis Figure 4.4 still 2.0 g and 1 M; Table C2 says 0.5 M and 3 (x 2) + 2. The text describes equilibrium around 2 h but does not explicitly reconcile duration labels.",
      "disposition": "retain contradictions; no corrected arm or mass-normalized yield"
    },
    {
      "id": "sampling",
      "locators": [
        "main2020 physical p5 methods",
        "thesis p116"
      ],
      "finding": "100 microlitre thief samples cumulatively no more than 1% of total volume are reported. Intermediate 250 mL rinse water was analyzed, called insignificant, and discarded. These statements do not provide sample-wise correction, rinse inventories or a closed original-feed balance.",
      "disposition": "bounded sampling description; raw assay/correction gap remains"
    },
    {
      "id": "column_flow",
      "locators": [
        "main2020 physical p5 methods",
        "main2020 physical pp12-13 Figures 5-6",
        "SI physical p16 / printed p15 Figure S33",
        "thesis pp116-117,126 Figure 4.5,127 Figure 4.6,129 Figure 4.7"
      ],
      "finding": "Article methods 1.00 BV/h versus article/SI captions 0.50 BV/h. Thesis methods and captions use 1.00 or 1.0 BV/h. Bed volume 5.50 mL; dry resin methods 1.79 g and captions 1.792 g. Fractions 0.5 BV. Agreement within the thesis is not proof of the actual rate underlying the published curves.",
      "disposition": "unresolved; do not silently prefer thesis"
    },
    {
      "id": "inlet_arm_mapping",
      "locators": [
        "main2020 physical p12 / article p11 Figure 5 and prose",
        "SI physical p16 / printed p15 Figure S33",
        "thesis p126 Figure 4.5, p127 Figure 4.6 and pp127-128 prose"
      ],
      "finding": "Article prose assigns 434 mg/L to fine A and 275 mg/L to coarse A, while fine Figure 5 plateaus near 275 and coarse Figure S33 near 430. Thesis explicitly labels fine A Ci=275 mg/L and coarse A Ci=434 mg/L; its prose agrees. This supports a provenance conflict, not automatic correction of the article or an independent measurement.",
      "disposition": "source-only conflict; no label swap in owner"
    },
    {
      "id": "mixing_loss",
      "locators": [
        "SI physical p14 / printed p13 Table S4",
        "thesis physical p241 / C14 Table C4"
      ],
      "finding": "SI mixes 25 mL caustic plus 25 mL acid; thesis mixes 250 mL plus 250 mL, at pH about 3. The same six precipitate masses occur in both: A fine 0.1039 g, A coarse 0.0993 g, B fine 0.0661 g, B coarse 0.0929 g, C fine 0.0748 g, C coarse 0.0759 g. These are mixed precipitate masses, not fluoride inventories; volume conflict prevents normalization.",
      "disposition": "no mixing-loss correction or pure cryolite yield"
    },
    {
      "id": "model_denominator",
      "locators": [
        "main2020 physical p6 methods, p14 / article p13",
        "SI printed pp3-4 model equations and p17 Table S5",
        "thesis p109, p117 methods, p127 Table 4.5, p130"
      ],
      "finding": "Recovery is main fluoride elution peak area divided by theoretical column uptake from dynamic model fitting. Article reports 59.0%; thesis adds 59.0 \u00b1 1.5%, still Dose-Response q0 based. Thesis total uptake 31.7/37.6 mg/g is calculated; first/second fine q0 5.01\u00b10.11 and 26.7\u00b10.4, coarse 4.23\u00b10.07 and 33.4\u00b10.7 mg/g match article/SI. No raw paired feed/wash/mix/residual/product inventory or uncertainty propagation was acquired.",
      "disposition": "model-dependent column metric, not original SPL recovery"
    },
    {
      "id": "replicates",
      "locators": [
        "main2020 physical p10 Figure 4, p12 Figure 5, p13 Figure 6",
        "thesis p124 Figure 4.4, p126 Figure 4.5, p129 Figure 4.7"
      ],
      "finding": "Leaching/loading captions describe 95% confidence limits from three electrode measurements; elution captions describe duplicate measurements. These are not evidence of three independent leaching/column experiments. Thesis \u00b11.5% does not establish an independently replicated whole-process yield.",
      "disposition": "preserve measurement-level replication"
    },
    {
      "id": "product_boundary",
      "locators": [
